The important limitation
Your current robot uses an Arduino Uno and a Bluetooth module. A backend hosted on Render cannot directly access Bluetooth hardware connected to your computer or phone. The Bluetooth connection must be handled by a device physically near the robot.

We have two possible designs:









Option A — Keep your current hardware

Use a website on your phone or computer and a small background bridge running on a nearby computer. The bridge communicates with the robot over Bluetooth. Remote control requires that bridge computer to remain on and connected.












Option B — Upgrade to Wi-Fi control

Use an ESP32 to connect the robot to Wi-Fi and communicate with the backend. This is a better architecture for remote access from different devices without relying on a Windows computer, although the robot still needs power and network connectivity.



The website can include separate Manual Control, Voice Control, and Auto Mode tabs. Voice recognition support varies by browser, and automatic operation must still run on a device connected to the robot.
